closed_at: "2026-08-24T16:39:33.996Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-24T16:39:33.996Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "Every read command contract publishes the exact projection modes accepted by runtime validation; The global degradation ladder is labeled as a union rather than a per-command guarantee; CLI full contracts, command-scoped contracts, MCP schemas, generated fixtures, and public SDK types stay byte-consistent; A contract consumer can select a valid projection for list and health without invoking either command; Negative controls fail when runtime modes and published modes diverge; Documentation explains modes, field selectors, and compatibility semantics within existing token ceilings"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Let agents choose a valid bounded-read projection without a failed exploratory call
value: "Contract discovery becomes executable, token-efficient, and identical to runtime validation across transports"
why_now: GitHub #1105 reproduced on the current release and the complete all-status lineage has no focused owner beyond the broad token-budget feature
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Published exact per-command projection vocabularies across shared SDK, CLI contracts, MCP discovery, generated fixtures, tests, and operator documentation."
expected_result: "pm contracts --command list and pm contracts --command health publish their exact supported projection modes and selector vocabulary, with CLI and MCP consumers reading the same SDK-owned declaration."
actual_result: "The SDK-owned read-output registry now publishes each command's exact projection_modes, runtime contracts expose a labeled global union plus command-scoped discovery metadata, and generated CLI/MCP/public SDK fixtures remain synchronized within existing token budgets."
affected_version: 2026.8.24
